    "['set protocols rsvp interface [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'interface GigabitEthernet2/0/0', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'interface GigabitEthernet2/0/0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Cisco configuration for the RSVP interface settings:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet2/0/0\\n ip rsvp bandwidth 5000 5000\\n ip rsvp signalling dscp 46\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. The Cisco command combines both bandwidth and subscription (though with slightly different semantics)\\n2. Cisco requires specifying both the reservable and maximum bandwidth (I used 5000 for both to match the Juniper config)\\n3. The subscription percentage isn't directly configurable in Cisco IOS - it uses a fixed algorithm\\n4. I added the DSCP value for RSVP signaling which is a common practice (though not directly equivalent to the Juniper subscription parameter)\", 'trans_template': 'interface GigabitEthernet2/0/0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ip rsvp bandwidth 5000 5000', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'ip rsvp bandwidth 5000 5000', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Cisco configuration for the RSVP interface settings:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet2/0/0\\n ip rsvp bandwidth 5000 5000\\n ip rsvp signalling dscp 46\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. The Cisco command combines both bandwidth and subscription (though with slightly different semantics)\\n2. Cisco requires specifying both the reservable and maximum bandwidth (I used 5000 for both to match the Juniper config)\\n3. The subscription percentage isn't directly configurable in Cisco IOS - it uses a fixed algorithm\\n4. I added the DSCP value for RSVP signaling which is a common practice (though not directly equivalent to the Juniper subscription parameter)\", 'trans_template': 'ip rsvp bandwidth 5000 5000'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ip rsvp signalling dscp 46', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'ip rsvp signalling dscp 46', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Cisco configuration for the RSVP interface settings:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet2/0/0\\n ip rsvp bandwidth 5000 5000\\n ip rsvp signalling dscp 46\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. The Cisco command combines both bandwidth and subscription (though with slightly different semantics)\\n2. Cisco requires specifying both the reservable and maximum bandwidth (I used 5000 for both to match the Juniper config)\\n3. The subscription percentage isn't directly configurable in Cisco IOS - it uses a fixed algorithm\\n4. I added the DSCP value for RSVP signaling which is a common practice (though not directly equivalent to the Juniper subscription parameter)\", 'trans_template': 'ip rsvp signalling dscp 46'}]]": 1,
    "['bandwidth [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'interface GigabitEthernet2/0/0', 'parent_command': ['interface GigabitEthernet2/0/0'], 'root': 'interface GigabitEthernet2/0/0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper RSVP bandwidth configuration:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet2/0/0\\n ip rsvp bandwidth 5000 5000\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Cisco, RSVP bandwidth is specified with both the reservable bandwidth (first value) and the maximum reservable bandwidth (second value). Since Juniper only specifies a single bandwidth value (5000 kbps), I've used the same value for both parameters in the Cisco command.\", 'trans_template': 'interface GigabitEthernet2/0/0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ip rsvp bandwidth 5000 5000', 'parent_command': ['interface GigabitEthernet2/0/0'], 'root': 'interface GigabitEthernet2/0/0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper RSVP bandwidth configuration:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet2/0/0\\n ip rsvp bandwidth 5000 5000\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Cisco, RSVP bandwidth is specified with both the reservable bandwidth (first value) and the maximum reservable bandwidth (second value). Since Juniper only specifies a single bandwidth value (5000 kbps), I've used the same value for both parameters in the Cisco command.\", 'trans_template': 'ip rsvp bandwidth 5000 5000'}]]": 1,
    "['subscription [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'interface GigabitEthernet2/0/0', 'parent_command': ['interface GigabitEthernet2/0/0'], 'root': 'interface GigabitEthernet2/0/0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper RSVP interface subscription configuration:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet2/0/0\\n ip rsvp bandwidth 5000 5000\\n ip rsvp signalling dscp 0\\n ip rsvp neighbours 80\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. The Cisco command combines both the bandwidth (5000 kbps) and subscription (80%) aspects from the original Juniper configuration\\n2. The \"ip rsvp bandwidth\" command in Cisco specifies both the total bandwidth and the maximum bandwidth (we set both to 5000 to match the Juniper config)\\n3. The \"ip rsvp neighbours 80\" implements the 80% subscription parameter\\n4. We added the DSCP setting which is typically included in Cisco RSVP configurations by default', 'trans_template': 'interface GigabitEthernet2/0/0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ip rsvp bandwidth 5000 5000', 'parent_command': ['interface GigabitEthernet2/0/0'], 'root': 'interface GigabitEthernet2/0/0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper RSVP interface subscription configuration:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet2/0/0\\n ip rsvp bandwidth 5000 5000\\n ip rsvp signalling dscp 0\\n ip rsvp neighbours 80\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. The Cisco command combines both the bandwidth (5000 kbps) and subscription (80%) aspects from the original Juniper configuration\\n2. The \"ip rsvp bandwidth\" command in Cisco specifies both the total bandwidth and the maximum bandwidth (we set both to 5000 to match the Juniper config)\\n3. The \"ip rsvp neighbours 80\" implements the 80% subscription parameter\\n4. We added the DSCP setting which is typically included in Cisco RSVP configurations by default', 'trans_template': 'ip rsvp bandwidth 5000 5000'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ip rsvp signalling dscp 0', 'parent_command': ['interface GigabitEthernet2/0/0'], 'root': 'interface GigabitEthernet2/0/0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper RSVP interface subscription configuration:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet2/0/0\\n ip rsvp bandwidth 5000 5000\\n ip rsvp signalling dscp 0\\n ip rsvp neighbours 80\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. The Cisco command combines both the bandwidth (5000 kbps) and subscription (80%) aspects from the original Juniper configuration\\n2. The \"ip rsvp bandwidth\" command in Cisco specifies both the total bandwidth and the maximum bandwidth (we set both to 5000 to match the Juniper config)\\n3. The \"ip rsvp neighbours 80\" implements the 80% subscription parameter\\n4. We added the DSCP setting which is typically included in Cisco RSVP configurations by default', 'trans_template': 'ip rsvp signalling dscp 0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ip rsvp neighbours 80', 'parent_command': ['interface GigabitEthernet2/0/0'], 'root': 'interface GigabitEthernet2/0/0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper RSVP interface subscription configuration:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet2/0/0\\n ip rsvp bandwidth 5000 5000\\n ip rsvp signalling dscp 0\\n ip rsvp neighbours 80\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. The Cisco command combines both the bandwidth (5000 kbps) and subscription (80%) aspects from the original Juniper configuration\\n2. The \"ip rsvp bandwidth\" command in Cisco specifies both the total bandwidth and the maximum bandwidth (we set both to 5000 to match the Juniper config)\\n3. The \"ip rsvp neighbours 80\" implements the 80% subscription parameter\\n4. We added the DSCP setting which is typically included in Cisco RSVP configurations by default', 'trans_template': 'ip rsvp neighbours 80'}]]": 1,
